# Document high-level changes in docs/

When you implement a **high-level** change (not a one-line bugfix), add or update markdown under [`docs/`](/work3/s204070/SPA/docs/) so the repo stays explainable without reading the diff.

## What counts as high-level

- New or changed **training / validation metrics**, checkpoint logic, or W&B logging
- New **experiments**, manifest blocks, cv4fold phases, or HPC submit workflows
- New **preprocessing** or audit pipelines
- **Architecture / conditioning** behavior that affects how runs are interpreted
- User-facing **workflows** (how to submit, postprocess, summarize results)

Skip docs for: typos, formatting, trivial renames, test-only fixes with no behavior change.

## Where to put docs

| Topic | Location |
|-------|----------|
| cv4fold, folds, tune winners, subject_lab | `docs/cv4fold/` — extend `README.md` or add a focused `.md` and link from README |
| cGMVAE / cHMM-GMVAE training, priors, losses | `docs/cgmvae_training.md`, `docs/cHMM_GMVAE.md`, or new `docs/cvae_*.md` |
| W&B metrics, checkpoint scores | `docs/cvae_wandb_checkpoint_metrics.md` |
| Preprocessing audit | `docs/preprocessing_audit_*.md` |
| Conditioning (subject / lab) | `docs/conditioning_story_map.md` |
| HPC submit / queues / wall times | `docs/HPC_SUBMIT_GUIDE.md` or `hpc/docs/` |
| CNN / data path | `docs/CNN_data_preprocessing.md` |

Prefer **one canonical doc per feature**; link from subsystem READMEs instead of duplicating tables.

## What to include

- **What changed** and **why** (1–2 sentences)
- **Config / YAML** knobs with defaults
- **W&B keys** or **result paths** if relevant
- **Code pointers** (main modules, not every file)
- **Date** or “Added YYYY-MM-DD” when useful for thesis timeline

## Agent workflow

1. Implement the change.
2. Create or update the doc in the same session (do not leave “TODO: document later”).
3. If `docs/cv4fold/README.md` (or similar index) lists workflows, add a **one-line link** to the new doc.
4. Do **not** edit `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md` unless the user asks.
